// The better bowler was WORSE, at everything, monotonically. The reason is
// arithmetic rather than cricket: raising one bowler's threat raised
// (batQ + bowlQ) / 2 on every ball he bowled, the standard term read that as
// higher-class cricket, and higher-class cricket scores more - so his own
// quality was handed to the man he was bowling at. A one-sided improvement must
// never move the standard, and if the standard is a property of the DELIVERY it
// always will.
